## Approach

Introduce an `AttributeRole` enum (`Identity`, `Obligation`) in `src/conventions/attributes.rs` and a classification function that maps every attribute string to its role. Add a `toolchain_enforced_pairs` method to the `FcaAttributeSource` trait so each language adapter can declare implications that the compiler/linter already enforces (e.g., Rust: `kind:function → naming:snake_case`). Use both to provide an `is_checkable` predicate on `Convention` that sutra/234 will call as a direction filter.

This is purely additive — no existing behavior changes. The filtering happens downstream in sutra/234's deviation report, not in the existing `FcaEngine::check` path (which is being replaced anyway).

