## Steps

### Step 1: Define `AttributeRole` enum and classifier in `attributes.rs`

Add the role enum and a function that classifies any attribute string. The classifier uses prefix matching on the known vocabulary.

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum AttributeRole {
    Identity,
    Obligation,
}

pub fn classify_attribute(attr: &str) -> AttributeRole {
    match attr {
        // Obligation: what a symbol should have/do
        "has_doc"
        | "is_async"
        | "returns_result"
        | "returns_option"
        | "returns_future" => AttributeRole::Obligation,
        a if a.starts_with("naming:") => AttributeRole::Obligation,
        a if a.starts_with("effect:") => AttributeRole::Obligation,

        // Identity: everything else — kind, vis, in, is_method, has_sig, complexity
        _ => AttributeRole::Identity,
    }
}
```

`vis:*` defaults to Identity (antecedent-only) per the task description — it's what a symbol *is* in terms of exposure, not what it *should* be. Note this call in a comment.

